SUMMARY:Bring your own telescope(BYOT)
DESCRIPTION:Have a telescope you’re not quite sure how to use\, or maybe you haven’t used in years? Bring it to this hands-on\, confidence-building workshop designed to help you get the most out of your stargazing experience! Whether you’ve just unboxed your first telescope or inherited a beloved but unfamiliar scope\, this class will give you the skills and understanding you need to explore the night sky with ease. \nWe’ll begin with a friendly\, beginner-focused introduction to the different types of telescopes\, how they work\, and the essential components you should know. You’ll learn practical tips on setup\, alignment\, focusing\, and how to navigate the sky—information that will help you avoid common frustrations and make your observing sessions far more enjoyable. \nAfter the overview\, you’ll receive dedicated one-on-one time with our knowledgeable docents\, who will work with you and your telescope directly. They’ll guide you step-by-step through operating\, troubleshooting issues\, and ensuring you feel completely comfortable using your equipment on your own. \nPlease Note: guests are strongly encouraged to email us prior to the event with your telescope specifications at info@rfo.org. This will help us ensure you get the help you need! \nWhether you’re hoping to see the rings of Saturn\, the craters of the Moon\, or deep-sky wonders far beyond\, this class will empower you to unlock the full potential of your telescope. Leave feeling inspired\, capable\, and ready for your next night under the stars!
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/bring-your-own-telescopebyot/
LOCATION:Robert Ferguson Observatory\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Road\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Kids and Family,Other,Recreation
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Robert Ferguson Observatory 2605 Adobe Canyon Road Kenwood CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2605 Adobe Canyon Road:geo:-122.533,38.4427
END:VEVENT
