SUMMARY:Exhibition Opening: Christo and Jeanne-Claude: Running Fence at 50 Years
DESCRIPTION:This landmark exhibition celebrates the 50th anniversary of Christo and Jeanne-Claude’s monumental Running Fence\, the temporary art installation that stretched over 24 miles through Sonoma and Marin Counties. The project became world famous\, and is an iconic part of North Bay culture and history. \nThrough immersive design\, powerful visuals\, and firsthand accounts\, the exhibit invites visitors to experience the magic and beauty that was the Running Fence – white fabric flowing across fields and cresting over hills to vanish into the Pacific Ocean – and to discover the remarkable 4-year odyssey that brought it to fruition. \nAdmission for sale at the door.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/exhibition-opening-christo-and-jeanne-claude-running-fence-at-50-years/
LOCATION:Museum of Sonoma County\, 425 7th St\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Art
GEO:38.441664;-122.718243
